// Module 10 quiz - Deep Learning for AI Startups
$CATEGORY: $course$/Module 10

::M10 Q1:: Why wrap a model in an API? {
~To make it more accurate
~To remove the need for data
=So other applications can call it#An API lets any program send a request over the network and get the model's answer back.
~To shrink the weights
}

::M10 Q2:: What does 95th percentile latency tell you? {
~The average time
=The time under which 95% of requests complete#One request in twenty is slower than this, so it shows the slow tail that users notice.
~The fastest request
~The number of users
}

::M10 Q3:: Which can reduce inference cost? {
~Sending longer prompts
~Using a larger model for every task
~Disabling logging only
=Caching repeated requests#A repeated input is answered from memory instead of being computed again, which saves time and compute.
}

::M10 Q4:: Why log inputs and outputs in production? {
=To monitor quality and debug problems, while respecting privacy#Logs show how the service behaves and where it fails, but private content should be hashed, shortened or left out.
~To slow the system
~To change the model weights directly
~To avoid testing
}

::M10 Q5:: Which tool is a quick way to build a web UI for a model demo? {
~A spreadsheet macro
~A compiler flag
=Gradio#Gradio turns a Python function into a web page in a few lines, and works with Hugging Face Spaces.
~A label editor
}
